A system and method are provided for dependable monitoring of a parameter—particularly a moment of inertia—used to calculate the kinetic energy of an object measurable by a sensor of a coordinate measuring machine. The object is transferred through multiple positions and preferably remains stationary, at least momentarily, at each approach position. The method includes:

a) obtaining an initial value of the parameter and designating it as the target value;

b) moving the object from one position to the subsequent position and recalculating the parameter for the movement cycle between those positions;

c) assigning the recalculated parameter as the actual value;

d) comparing the actual value with the target value;

e) when the actual value substantially matches the target value, continuing to move the object and repeating step b) until the final position is reached; or

f) when the actual value differs significantly from the target value, generating an error message.
